<style>
  /* As this is a demo page just show the entire conversation without scrolling */
  .l-ui-page:has(.l-ui-conversation__container) {
    max-height: none;
    overflow: visible;
  }
</style>

<h1>Conversations</h1>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">A message list component for displaying conversations and messages. The container uses <code>flex-1 min-h-0</code> to fill available space within a flex parent. When placed inside an <code>l-ui-page</code>, the page is automatically constrained to viewport height so messages scroll within the available space while the composer stays pinned at the bottom. If you have a title bar or other content above the messages, include it inside the container so the remaining height is calculated correctly.</p>

<div class="l-ui-conversation__container l-ui-utility--mt-xl">
  <div class="l-ui-conversation__messages">
    <div class="l-ui-conversation">
      <div class="l-ui-message">
        <div class="l-ui-message__avatar">AL</div>
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__author">Alice</div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__body">
            Has anyone had a chance to review the pull request? I'd love to get it merged before the end of the week.
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">10:30 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-message--sent">
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__author">Bob</div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__body">
            I'll take a look this afternoon. The changes look straightforward from the description.
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__metadata">Claude Opus 4.6 (~128 tokens)</div>
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">10:32 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-message">
        <div class="l-ui-message__avatar">AL</div>
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__author">Alice</div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__body">
            Thank you! Let me know if you have any questions about the implementation.
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__metadata">ChatGPT 5.2 (~96 tokens)</div>
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">10:33 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-conversation__separator">Today</div>

      <div class="l-ui-message">
        <div class="l-ui-message__avatar">BK</div>
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__author">Bob</div>
          <details class="l-ui-message__reasoning">
            <summary class="l-ui-message__reasoning-summary"><%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_chevron_right.svg", class: "l-ui-icon--sm", alt: "" %> Reasoning</summary>
            <div class="l-ui-message__reasoning-body">
              The user is asking me to review a pull request. Let me look at the key changes... The validate_input method currently accepts any string, but doesn't guard against nil or empty values. This could cause a NoMethodError in production. I should also check the error messages - they're quite generic right now.
            </div>
          </details>
          <div class="l-ui-message__body l-ui-markdown">
            <p>I left a few comments on the PR. The main issue is the <code>validate_input</code> method - it doesn't handle <strong>empty strings</strong> or <code>nil</code> values. Here's what I'd suggest:</p>
            <pre><code>def validate_input(value)
  return false if value.nil? || value.empty?
  value.match?(/\A[\w\s]+\z/)
end</code></pre>
            <p>Also, the error messages could be more descriptive. Instead of <em>"invalid input"</em>, something like:</p>
            <blockquote>
              <p>Please enter a value containing only letters, numbers, and spaces.</p>
            </blockquote>
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__metadata">Claude Opus 4.6 (~215 tokens)</div>
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">10:45 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-message--sent">
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__body l-ui-markdown">
            <p>Good catches, Bob. I agree with both suggestions. To summarise the changes needed:</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Add <strong>nil and empty string</strong> guards to <code>validate_input</code></li>
              <li>Update error messages to be more descriptive</li>
              <li>Add unit tests for the new edge cases</li>
            </ol>
            <p>I'll push a fix shortly.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__metadata">ChatGPT 5.2 (~84 tokens)</div>
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">11:02 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-message">
        <div class="l-ui-message__avatar">AL</div>
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-message__author">Alice</div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__body l-ui-markdown">
            <p>I've pushed the fix. Here's what changed:</p>
            <h3>Validation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Added <s>early return</s> guard clause for <code>nil</code> and empty strings</li>
              <li>Improved the regex to also allow <em>hyphens</em> and <em>underscores</em></li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Error messages</h3>
            <table>
              <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Error message changes</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Before</th>
                  <th scope="col">After</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>invalid input</code></td>
                  <td>Please enter a valid name</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><code>too long</code></td>
                  <td>Name must be under 255 characters</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <hr>
            <p>Ready for re-review when you get a chance.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="l-ui-message__footer">
            <div class="l-ui-message__metadata">ChatGPT 5.2 (~340 tokens)</div>
            <div class="l-ui-message__timestamp">11:30 AM</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="l-ui-message">
        <div class="l-ui-message__avatar">BK</div>
        <div class="l-ui-message__bubble">
          <div class="l-ui-typing-indicator" role="status">
            <span class="l-ui-sr-only">Someone is typing</span>
            <div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"></div>
            <div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"></div>
            <div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="l-ui-conversation__composer">
    <textarea class="l-ui-conversation__composer-input" placeholder="Type a message..." rows="1" aria-label="Type a message"></textarea>
    <button class="l-ui-button--primary">Send</button>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="l-ui-utility--mt-xl" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button--outline" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-conversations-container-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-conversations-container-heading">Conversation container</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <%= image_tag "layered_ui/icon_close.svg", alt: "", class: "l-ui-icon--sm", aria: { hidden: true } %>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <pre class="l-ui-surface"><code>&lt;div class="l-ui-conversation__container"&gt;
  &lt;div class="l-ui-conversation__messages"&gt;
    &lt;div class="l-ui-conversation"&gt;
      &lt;!-- Plain text message --&gt;
      &lt;div class="l-ui-message"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="l-ui-message--sent"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;!-- Message with reasoning --&gt;
      &lt;div class="l-ui-message"&gt;
        &lt;div class="l-ui-message__avatar"&gt;BK&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="l-ui-message__bubble"&gt;
          &lt;details class="l-ui-message__reasoning"&gt;
            &lt;summary class="l-ui-message__reasoning-summary"&gt;
              &lt;svg class="l-ui-icon--sm"&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;
              Reasoning
            &lt;/summary&gt;
            &lt;div class="l-ui-message__reasoning-body"&gt;
              Streamed reasoning text...
            &lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/details&gt;
          &lt;div class="l-ui-message__body l-ui-markdown"&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;Rendered HTML from markdown...&lt;/p&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;

      &lt;!-- Typing indicator --&gt;
      &lt;div class="l-ui-message"&gt;
        &lt;div class="l-ui-message__avatar"&gt;BK&lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;div class="l-ui-message__bubble"&gt;
          &lt;div class="l-ui-typing-indicator"&gt;
            &lt;div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;div class="l-ui-typing-indicator__dot"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
          &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="l-ui-conversation__composer"&gt;
    &lt;textarea class="l-ui-conversation__composer-input"
      placeholder="Type a message..." rows="1"&gt;
    &lt;/textarea&gt;
    &lt;button class="l-ui-button--primary"&gt;Send&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

